  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of length NNN.\n\nYour task is to find any three indices i,j,ki, j, ki,j,k such that:\n\n\n1≤i,j,k≤N1 \\le i, j, k \\le N1≤i,j,k≤N\ni≠j,i≠k,j≠ki \\ne j, i \\ne k, j \\ne ki=j,i=k,j=k\n\nThat is, the indices {i,j,k}\\{i, j, k\\}{i,j,k} are pairwise distinct.\nAi+Aj≠AkA_i + A_j \\ne A_kAi​+Aj​=Ak​\nIf there are multiple possible solutions, you may find any of them.\n\nIf no solution exists, print −1-1−1.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the length of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case,\n\n\n\nIf no solution exists, output the single integer −1-1−1.\nOtherwise, output three distinct space-separated integers i,j,ki, j, ki,j,k denoting the indices you found.\n\nIf there are multiple solutions, any of them will be accepted.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤3⋅1041 \\leq T \\leq 3\\cdot 10^41≤T≤3⋅104",
      "3≤N≤2⋅1053 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^53≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤Ai≤1080 \\le A_i \\le 10^80≤Ai​≤108",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n4\n2 1 3 0\n3\n0 0 0\n4\n4 2 0 2",
        "output": "4 2 1\n-1\n2 3 1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: With (i,j,k)=(4,2,1)(i, j, k) = (4, 2, 1)(i,j,k)=(4,2,1), we have A4=0,A2=1,A1=2A_4 = 0, A_2 = 1, A_1 = 2A4​=0,A2​=1,A1​=2.\nBecause 0+1≠20+1\\ne 20+1=2, this is a valid triplet.\nThere are many several other valid solutions, which will all be accepted as well.\nTest case 222: It can be verified that no valid triplet of indices exists.\nTest case 333: Consider (i,j,k)=(2,3,1)(i, j, k) = (2, 3, 1)(i,j,k)=(2,3,1), which gives Ai+Aj=A2+A3=2A_i + A_j = A_2 + A_3 = 2Ai​+Aj​=A2​+A3​=2 while Ak=A1=4A_k = A_1 = 4Ak​=A1​=4.\nBecause 2≠42\\ne 42=4 this is a valid triplet."
      }
    ]
  },
